#
# ESP System Settings
#
# Native machine code (CIRCUITPY_ENABLE_MPY_NATIVE=1) is copied into RAM and
# executed from there. The PMS/PMP memory protection marks all RAM
# non-executable and makes MALLOC_CAP_EXEC allocations fail, so it has to be
# off for native code to run. This lowers a security boundary: a bug that can
# write RAM can then also run code from it. Only pulled in by the Makefile
# when the flag is set.
# CONFIG_ESP_SYSTEM_MEMPROT is not set
# end of ESP System Settings

# end of Component config

# end of Espressif IoT Development Framework Configuration
